  <result type="2">
   <title>
    <narrative xml:lang="EN">Member States in the Security Council, and the UN system, is empowered to understand and act on the consequences of climate change for peace and security through evidenced-based information and analysis on climate-related peace and security risks in selected countries and regions on the agenda of the UNSC.</narrative>
   </title>
   <reference code="279895" vocabulary="99"></reference>
   <indicator aggregation-status="0" ascending="1" measure="1">
    <title>
     <narrative xml:lang="EN">Survey feedback from diplomats and UN staff on the usefulness of the fact sheets and research reports produced by the project, with specific information on the ways in which the information and analyses contained in the fact sheets and reports was used in UNSC product drafting and negotiations, and how they were used to develop knowledge, policies and programming more generally.

In addition, outcomes indicators could include: 
&#x2022;	References by UN member states to factsheets in different UN foras, e.g. UNSC, IEG, GoF, etc.
&#x2022;	Sustained interest of UN member states in attending factsheet launch events  (and positive feedback during or subsequently on the usefulness of the factsheets)
&#x2022;	Opening rate of factsheet dissemination email, website visits, downloads, social media interest
&#x2022;	Evidence of sustained knowledge of UN member states on CPS in countries covered in factsheets, including through implicit or explicit references to NUPI-SIPRI factsheets.</narrative>
    </title>
